1
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:45,962
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

2
00:00:51,134 --> 00:00:53,762
‎EMERGENCY SERVICES

3
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:04,856
‎Female in her thirties,
‎car accident victim.

4
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:06,524
‎We found her unconscious

5
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:08,401
‎with an initial blood pressure
‎of 100 over 80.

6
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,404
‎Now it's 80 over 56 and falling.

7
00:01:14,783 --> 00:01:15,700
‎Mr. Ma.

8
00:01:17,327 --> 00:01:18,787
‎-Mr. Ma!
‎-What's wrong?

9
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,205
‎-What's happening?
‎-Mr. Ma.

10
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:21,790
‎-Is he okay?
‎-He needs help!

11
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:25,001
‎-Mr. Ma, what's wrong?
‎-What's wrong, Gang-uk?

12
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:30,089
‎I need more suction.

13
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:36,888
‎Keep them coming.

14
00:01:36,971 --> 00:01:38,473
‎-Anesthesiologist, what's her BP?
‎-Yes?

15
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:42,101
‎-It's stable at 100 over 60.
‎-Suction.

16
00:01:42,727 --> 00:01:44,312
‎-Keep an eye on the BP.
‎-Will do.

17
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,105
‎I need more suction.

18
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:47,023
‎RESTRICTED AREA

19
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:48,316
‎EPISODE 12

20
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:50,485
‎-You all must've been shocked.
‎-Yes.

21
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,946
‎I'll cut to the chase.

22
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:55,406
‎It wasn't an issue
‎with the transplanted heart.

23
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:58,118
‎It was hyperventilation
‎caused by excessive stress.

24
00:02:00,411 --> 00:02:01,538
‎Oh, thank you.

25
00:02:01,621 --> 00:02:04,332
‎If he goes into shock
‎and hyperventilates again like today,

26
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:05,500
‎it could cause arrhythmia.

27
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,377
‎He needs complete rest for now.

28
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:09,254
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

29
00:02:09,796 --> 00:02:11,840
‎-Thank you, doctor.
‎-Thank you.

30
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:14,509
‎My goodness…

31
00:02:14,592 --> 00:02:16,594
‎That gave you quite a scare, didn't it?

32
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:19,514
‎It's a relief though.

33
00:02:26,938 --> 00:02:29,023
‎-Gang-uk.
‎-Mr. Ma.

34
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,527
‎What is it? No, keep still.

35
00:02:35,905 --> 00:02:38,491
‎Yeo-ri. What about Yeo-ri?

36
00:02:45,498 --> 00:02:47,250
‎-No, you can't…
‎-Gang-uk.

37
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,878
‎-You can't leave like this, Mr. Ma.
‎-Wait…

38
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:56,050
‎I'm afraid you should
‎prepare yourselves for the worst.

39
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:11,524
‎Gang-uk!

40
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:33,463
‎What if Yeo-ri never wakes up?

41
00:03:33,546 --> 00:03:35,131
‎I feel weird about this.

42
00:03:35,214 --> 00:03:37,383
‎They say life has its ups and downs.

43
00:03:39,052 --> 00:03:41,012
‎To think this would happen to her,

44
00:03:41,095 --> 00:03:43,514
‎who seemed so confident
‎at the extraordinary general meeting…

45
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:45,683
‎It's probably

46
00:03:46,809 --> 00:03:48,561
‎for the best if we stay away, right?

47
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:50,730
‎There's the issue of her succession,

48
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:54,901
‎so we should lie low
‎and try to stay under the radar.

49
00:03:58,404 --> 00:04:00,823
‎KOREA BARUM MEDICAL CENTER

50
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:08,623
‎It's all my fault.

51
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:12,502
‎If it weren't for me…

52
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:16,381
‎Why would you say something like that?

53
00:04:16,464 --> 00:04:19,884
‎Ms. Cheon will wake up soon.
‎Try not to worry too much.

54
00:04:20,551 --> 00:04:21,678
‎So Mr. Ma,

55
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:24,347
‎go home and get some rest.

56
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:27,392
‎Yeah, take care of yourself
‎so you can look after Yeo-ri.

57
00:04:28,309 --> 00:04:30,103
‎If you end up hyperventilating again,

58
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,272
‎-it could damage your heart.
‎-He's right.

59
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:34,899
‎I heard arrhythmia can be fatal
‎for heart transplant patients.

60
00:04:35,483 --> 00:04:36,693
‎Gosh, your grandmother

61
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:38,861
‎must've been so shaken up.

62
00:04:42,115 --> 00:04:43,032
‎You can go on home.

63
00:04:45,201 --> 00:04:47,328
‎Look after yourself, okay?

64
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:50,290
‎Gang-uk is fine now.

65
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:56,587
‎Fortunately for him,
‎his transplanted heart wasn't the problem.

66
00:04:57,588 --> 00:04:59,841
‎That heart is such a precious gift.

67
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,884
‎For Ji-hwan's sake,

68
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:04,387
‎I won't allow anything to happen to it.

69
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,431
‎Yes.

70
00:05:06,514 --> 00:05:08,933
‎You don't have to worry, ma'am.

71
00:05:09,559 --> 00:05:11,602
‎I'll be in touch.

72
00:05:12,145 --> 00:05:13,980
‎Yes. Take care, Ms. Song.

73
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:15,398
‎Bye.

74
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:20,778
‎Grandma.

75
00:05:21,821 --> 00:05:23,406
‎Oh, Gang-uk.

76
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:25,950
‎Was the person who gave me their heart

77
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:28,786
‎someone named Ji-hwan?

78
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:32,957
‎Yes.

79
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:34,542
‎And by Ms. Song…

80
00:05:36,169 --> 00:05:37,837
‎do you mean the lady we had lunch with?

81
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,758
‎Now that it's come to this,

82
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:43,843
‎I guess I can't keep it from you.

83
00:05:44,802 --> 00:05:46,637
‎The heart you were given

84
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:52,226
‎belonged to the son of the woman
‎we had lunch with.

85
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:59,734
‎So the person
‎you always had me pray for at the temple…

86
00:05:59,817 --> 00:06:01,235
‎That was Ji-hwan.

87
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:02,737
‎Yes.

88
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:05,531
‎You know CL Group, don't you?

89
00:06:06,407 --> 00:06:09,327
‎Ms. Song is
‎the vice president of CL Group,

90
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:12,955
‎and Ji-hwan was her younger son.

91
00:06:13,539 --> 00:06:15,249
‎If it's CL Group…

92
00:06:16,709 --> 00:06:18,586
‎then he was Kang Min-hwan's brother?

93
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:24,300
‎I was in a yacht accident
‎when I was in university.

94
00:06:42,485 --> 00:06:45,363
‎If our lives changed track
‎because of this pendant,

95
00:06:46,405 --> 00:06:47,657
‎then that means

96
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:50,660
‎Ji-hwan really died because of me.

97
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:53,538
‎Since it was given to you,

98
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:56,040
‎you should hold onto it.

99
00:08:34,096 --> 00:08:35,181
‎Jang Eun-ju?

100
00:08:37,808 --> 00:08:39,727
‎Will you please help me?

101
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:07,004
‎Goodbye, to a better place.

102
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,662
‎I'm here at last.

103
00:10:25,374 --> 00:10:27,293
‎Forgive me for taking so long to come.

104
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:30,046
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN

105
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:32,298
‎I thought to myself every morning

106
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,384
‎that I'd live a life…

107
00:10:37,637 --> 00:10:39,597
‎that wouldn't disappoint my donor.

108
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:53,694
‎I came

109
00:10:54,612 --> 00:10:56,030
‎to return this to you.

110
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:58,991
‎I heard it belonged to you.

111
00:11:00,951 --> 00:11:01,911
‎The time you gave

112
00:11:02,787 --> 00:11:04,163
‎Yeo-ri and me

113
00:11:05,247 --> 00:11:06,666
‎was a precious gift.

114
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:10,419
‎Thank you for granting it,

115
00:11:11,921 --> 00:11:13,005
‎and I'm sorry it happened.

116
00:11:15,341 --> 00:11:16,592
‎But now…

117
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:20,846
‎I'm afraid Yeo-ri will leave me.

118
00:11:24,892 --> 00:11:27,061
‎I want to do anything I can for her…

119
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,441
‎but there's nothing I can do.

120
00:11:34,568 --> 00:11:36,570
‎Then the pendant came to mind.

121
00:11:38,906 --> 00:11:41,200
‎If I were to return it
‎to its rightful owner…

122
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:44,912
‎then perhaps Yeo-ri might come back.

123
00:11:47,540 --> 00:11:49,250
‎I'm here because I'm desperate.

124
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:56,632
‎I'm begging you.

125
00:12:00,886 --> 00:12:02,721
‎Please help Yeo-ri come back.

126
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,226
‎Please.

127
00:12:09,186 --> 00:12:10,187
‎Please…

128
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:21,926
‎Prepare to intubate.

129
00:13:46,367 --> 00:13:47,284
‎Ji-hwan.

130
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:51,622
‎Hold on.

131
00:13:56,293 --> 00:13:58,045
‎We have a pulse.

132
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:03,551
‎Thank you.

133
00:14:05,344 --> 00:14:06,428
‎Thank you.

134
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:12,142
‎Ji-hwan.

135
00:14:15,145 --> 00:14:16,647
‎So we meet again here.

136
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:20,359
‎I'm sorry…

137
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,238
‎for living

138
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:26,949
‎in your place.

139
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:30,536
‎I'm so sorry.

140
00:14:31,036 --> 00:14:31,871
‎Don't be.

141
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,081
‎I told you

142
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:36,876
‎that I'd die in your place
‎so you can live.

143
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:46,176
‎Does this mean

144
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:50,931
‎it's time for me to go where I belong?

145
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:52,933
‎Yeo-ri.

146
00:14:55,686 --> 00:14:56,979
‎You can't get on this boat.

147
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,533
‎You offered your hand to others.

148
00:15:15,331 --> 00:15:17,750
‎They all came here to repay the warmth

149
00:15:18,417 --> 00:15:19,710
‎you showed them.

150
00:15:23,964 --> 00:15:24,840
‎That warmth

151
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:28,177
‎is what kept you from crossing over.

152
00:15:31,889 --> 00:15:33,265
‎And more than anything…

153
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:43,067
‎There are those

154
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:46,612
‎who will never let go of your hand,
‎no matter what.

155
00:15:51,200 --> 00:15:53,786
‎Those wishing for you to come back
‎more than anything.

156
00:15:57,206 --> 00:15:58,999
‎They're surrounding you with their warmth.

157
00:16:05,965 --> 00:16:07,174
‎Go back, Yeo-ri.

158
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:09,385
‎Then…

159
00:16:13,681 --> 00:16:14,723
‎what about you?

160
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:17,559
‎This time,

161
00:16:18,769 --> 00:16:19,895
‎you must go on your own.

162
00:16:23,023 --> 00:16:24,066
‎You've been through a lot

163
00:16:26,026 --> 00:16:27,194
‎because of me.

164
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:30,739
‎I'll go back to where I belong now.

165
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:37,955
‎Thank you.

166
00:16:40,499 --> 00:16:41,917
‎Thank you, Ji-hwan.

167
00:16:46,755 --> 00:16:47,589
‎I'm thankful

168
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:49,466
‎for you too.

169
00:18:03,165 --> 00:18:04,166
‎Yeo-ri?

170
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:23,018
‎You're back, right?

171
00:19:22,202 --> 00:19:23,787
‎Any news on Cheon Yeo-ri's condition?

172
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:26,081
‎She's been in a coma for a week.

173
00:19:26,623 --> 00:19:28,834
‎Prosecutor Ma Gang-uk
‎has been staying by her side.

174
00:19:31,628 --> 00:19:32,713
‎What about the police?

175
00:19:32,796 --> 00:19:35,716
‎We've handled the surveillance cameras,
‎and they're not up to much

176
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,384
‎after ruling the driver responsible.

177
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,514
‎Check the guest routes for the memorial
‎and rehearse every step

178
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:44,016
‎to ensure a smooth process.

179
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:45,642
‎I'll oversee

180
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:47,936
‎the final inspection myself.

181
00:19:48,020 --> 00:19:48,896
‎Yes, sir.

182
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,490
‎-Thank you.
‎-Thank you.

183
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,454
‎Help me sit up, Gang-uk.

184
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,832
‎You should lie down a little longer.

185
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:10,334
‎I feel fine.

186
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:14,129
‎The doctor said I need to move a bit
‎if I want to recover.

187
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,719
‎I have something to ask you.

188
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:24,014
‎The site of the car accident.

189
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:27,226
‎How did you know I was there?

190
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:30,938
‎Ji-hwan told me.

191
00:20:33,649 --> 00:20:35,275
‎I was able to come back

192
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:37,986
‎because he sent me back.

193
00:20:40,739 --> 00:20:41,573
‎To tell you the truth,

194
00:20:42,574 --> 00:20:44,243
‎I went to see him too.

195
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:49,248
‎Ji-hwan was the donor
‎who gave me his heart.

196
00:20:51,083 --> 00:20:53,168
‎I found out by chance

197
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,586
‎while you were unconscious.

198
00:20:58,340 --> 00:20:59,299
‎So Ji-hwan…

199
00:21:02,219 --> 00:21:03,095
‎saved

200
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:06,848
‎both you and me.

201
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:12,271
‎I returned the pendant to him too.

202
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:16,275
‎I had to do something for you,

203
00:21:16,858 --> 00:21:18,819
‎but I just didn't know what.

204
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,321
‎So I thought returning the pendant

205
00:21:22,572 --> 00:21:24,283
‎might help you come back.

206
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:28,203
‎I guess that's why
‎I was able to come back.

207
00:21:29,329 --> 00:21:30,622
‎Thank you.

208
00:21:32,374 --> 00:21:34,042
‎I'm so glad you're back.

209
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:39,256
‎I could wish for nothing more

210
00:21:40,549 --> 00:21:41,883
‎as long as you're with me.

211
00:21:58,567 --> 00:22:01,194
‎No, it's fine. Just stay put.

212
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:03,488
‎It's okay.

213
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:10,662
‎Dr. Han says you're recovering fast.

214
00:22:12,289 --> 00:22:13,582
‎That's good to hear.

215
00:22:14,374 --> 00:22:16,251
‎Well, Yeo-ri.

216
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:17,961
‎Yes?

217
00:22:18,045 --> 00:22:21,214
‎Knowing you got hurt
‎trying to save Gang-uk,

218
00:22:21,798 --> 00:22:23,717
‎I feel so terrible.

219
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:26,345
‎Please don't.

220
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:28,347
‎One's sincerity comes before

221
00:22:29,181 --> 00:22:30,432
‎any superstition.

222
00:22:31,058 --> 00:22:32,934
‎I've lived to this age
‎and failed to see that.

223
00:22:34,394 --> 00:22:37,606
‎I'm deeply sorry for what I said.

224
00:22:38,982 --> 00:22:40,192
‎You don't have to be, ma'am.

225
00:22:40,275 --> 00:22:46,114
‎I wish for nothing more
‎than for you two to be happy together.

226
00:22:46,198 --> 00:22:47,032
‎I mean it.

227
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:50,452
‎Good. And delete Shaman Sim's number.

228
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,954
‎I trust you will manage fine now.

229
00:22:53,038 --> 00:22:53,955
‎I do.

230
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:59,252
‎Why do we have to keep it a secret
‎that you're awake?

231
00:23:01,379 --> 00:23:04,883
‎Something about the accident bothers me.

232
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:07,177
‎For now, I want Director Lee

233
00:23:07,260 --> 00:23:09,888
‎to step in as Reina Hotel's acting CEO.

234
00:23:11,598 --> 00:23:12,682
‎Trust me on this.

235
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:29,991
‎-She must be seriously--
‎-Oh, my goodness!

236
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:31,952
‎What are you doing here, Ha-ri?

237
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:33,453
‎Why are ‎you‎ here, Mom?

238
00:23:34,079 --> 00:23:36,206
‎-You said you were too busy to--
‎-You traitors.

239
00:23:36,289 --> 00:23:37,707
‎Fancy seeing you both here.

240
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:41,545
‎You said we should lie low
‎and stay under the radar.

241
00:23:41,628 --> 00:23:44,798
‎What about you?
‎You said it would be best to stay away.

242
00:23:44,881 --> 00:23:45,715
‎Hey.

243
00:23:46,299 --> 00:23:49,427
‎After all, she's in a coma
‎after being hit by a truck.

244
00:23:49,511 --> 00:23:51,596
‎It would look bad
‎if we didn't care at all.

245
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:55,475
‎And I just felt bad.
‎It felt wrong to ignore her, you know?

246
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:58,687
‎Exactly. I guess there's a thin line
‎between love and hate.

247
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:01,439
‎They say blood is thicker than water.

248
00:24:01,523 --> 00:24:04,025
‎And as a fellow parent,

249
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:06,236
‎I was worried about the chairwoman too.

250
00:24:06,319 --> 00:24:07,362
‎Okay.

251
00:24:07,445 --> 00:24:08,905
‎Since we're here anyway,

252
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:10,448
‎let's pay her a visit together.

253
00:24:10,532 --> 00:24:11,825
‎You lead the way, Mom.

254
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:22,502
‎It's okay.

255
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:25,005
‎We're okay.

256
00:24:35,265 --> 00:24:37,392
‎Is she gone? Is she?

257
00:24:37,475 --> 00:24:39,978
‎Why are we hiding
‎when we came to wish her well?

258
00:24:41,313 --> 00:24:42,230
‎Well…

259
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:44,524
‎Seeing the chairwoman all of a sudden

260
00:24:44,608 --> 00:24:46,860
‎reminded me of
‎the extraordinary general meeting.

261
00:24:46,943 --> 00:24:49,154
‎I guess I felt guilty for what I did.

262
00:24:49,237 --> 00:24:51,865
‎That's all the more reason
‎we should get on their good books.

263
00:24:51,948 --> 00:24:54,326
‎Man, it was a great opportunity
‎and we ruined it by hiding.

264
00:24:54,409 --> 00:24:55,952
‎You were the first to hide.

265
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,120
‎I was just…

266
00:24:57,204 --> 00:24:59,748
‎He takes after me,
‎so he has fast reflexes.

267
00:24:59,831 --> 00:25:02,125
‎Oh, I don't know.
‎I must've felt guilty too.

268
00:25:02,209 --> 00:25:05,045
‎What now? Do we go in or not?

269
00:25:05,128 --> 00:25:06,796
‎Let me think for a second.

270
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:08,256
‎We need to calm down first.

271
00:25:11,468 --> 00:25:12,969
‎Anything on the truck driver?

272
00:25:13,553 --> 00:25:15,764
‎He insists he fell asleep at the wheel.

273
00:25:15,847 --> 00:25:18,350
‎Pil-dong.
‎I know for sure he didn't doze off.

274
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:19,517
‎Right.

275
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:22,812
‎I read the investigation report,
‎and there weren't any skid marks.

276
00:25:22,896 --> 00:25:23,730
‎See?

277
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:25,232
‎There's nothing.

278
00:25:25,815 --> 00:25:27,943
‎-Is my bag still missing?
‎-Yeah.

279
00:25:28,610 --> 00:25:31,821
‎Why didn't the cameras work that night?
‎I mean, we're looking into it…

280
00:25:31,905 --> 00:25:33,198
‎Could someone have taken it?

281
00:25:33,281 --> 00:25:35,700
‎There was a cuff link in my bag.

282
00:25:35,784 --> 00:25:37,327
‎Someone could've

283
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:39,788
‎caused the accident
‎to get their hands on it.

284
00:25:39,871 --> 00:25:43,458
‎So you're saying
‎the person who killed Park Seung-jae

285
00:25:43,541 --> 00:25:44,960
‎was responsible for the accident too?

286
00:25:45,043 --> 00:25:46,294
‎No.

287
00:25:46,378 --> 00:25:48,838
‎I doubt they did it themselves.
‎They must've hired someone.

288
00:25:53,969 --> 00:25:54,886
‎Hey, Yeo-ri.

289
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,392
‎I wish you'd stay
‎in the hospital a bit longer.

290
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:02,686
‎Are you sure you'll be okay?

291
00:26:03,186 --> 00:26:04,020
‎Yes.

292
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:08,108
‎I was so close
‎to never coming back home.

293
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:10,277
‎It feels strange to be back.

294
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:11,861
‎Sit down carefully.

295
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,242
‎I'm really okay now.

296
00:26:21,621 --> 00:26:22,664
‎How are things?

297
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,208
‎You still don't see ghosts anymore?

298
00:26:27,377 --> 00:26:28,837
‎What about you, Gang-uk?

299
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,547
‎You held my bare hand.

300
00:26:31,548 --> 00:26:32,382
‎I don't see them.

301
00:26:36,553 --> 00:26:37,470
‎Then I guess

302
00:26:39,097 --> 00:26:41,141
‎I won't see them ever again.

303
00:26:43,476 --> 00:26:44,853
‎That's such a relief.

304
00:26:54,195 --> 00:26:57,407
‎I'd like a coffee.
‎It's been a while since I had one.

305
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:58,700
‎You can't have one, Yeo-ri.

306
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:01,911
‎The doctor said absolutely no caffeine
‎for the time being.

307
00:27:04,122 --> 00:27:05,206
‎Drink this instead.

308
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:15,091
‎Just wait until I catch
‎whoever did that to you.

309
00:27:17,635 --> 00:27:19,929
‎It wasn't an ordinary accident, was it?

310
00:27:20,555 --> 00:27:21,389
‎No.

311
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:24,392
‎Don't you think
‎whoever killed Park Seung-jae

312
00:27:24,476 --> 00:27:26,519
‎is somehow involved in this too?

313
00:27:27,020 --> 00:27:29,230
‎It's likely that Park was killed

314
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,107
‎by the person he tried to blackmail.

315
00:27:31,691 --> 00:27:33,360
‎The yacht accident was 12 years ago,

316
00:27:33,443 --> 00:27:36,863
‎so it's strange that he tried to blackmail
‎after all this time.

317
00:27:37,489 --> 00:27:38,948
‎Do you think he found out something

318
00:27:39,032 --> 00:27:41,743
‎while he was out for the funeral?

319
00:27:41,826 --> 00:27:43,411
‎I traced Park Seung-jae's movements,

320
00:27:43,495 --> 00:27:45,580
‎and he'd gone to his childhood home.

321
00:27:46,122 --> 00:27:48,875
‎It was practically empty
‎since his father lived there alone

322
00:27:48,958 --> 00:27:50,293
‎until his recent death.

323
00:27:51,461 --> 00:27:52,754
‎Did anything noteworthy come up?

324
00:27:52,837 --> 00:27:55,924
‎The police did an initial inspection
‎but found nothing interesting.

325
00:28:01,179 --> 00:28:02,013
‎Yeo-ri.

326
00:28:02,806 --> 00:28:05,600
‎Don't worry too much.
‎I'll take care of it.

327
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:08,937
‎Just focus on recovering, okay?

328
00:28:09,020 --> 00:28:11,731
‎You should be careful out there, Gang-uk.

329
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:13,691
‎The culprit's still out there.

330
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:15,735
‎Okay.

331
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:34,587
‎We just need to set up the centerpiece,
‎and we'll be set.

332
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:36,756
‎Okay.

333
00:28:38,508 --> 00:28:39,342
‎Min-hwan?

334
00:28:40,635 --> 00:28:41,469
‎Mother.

335
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:50,645
‎Aren't you too busy
‎to handle the memorial ceremony?

336
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:53,398
‎This should be
‎my first priority, and it is.

337
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:56,359
‎-We're remembering my brother, Ji-hwan.
‎-Right.

338
00:28:56,943 --> 00:29:01,030
‎I'm sure Ji-hwan feels loved
‎even from the other side,

339
00:29:01,114 --> 00:29:04,033
‎with an older brother like you
‎looking out for him.

340
00:29:05,452 --> 00:29:06,911
‎-Shall we take a walk?
‎-Sure.

341
00:29:09,122 --> 00:29:09,956
‎By the way,

342
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:13,042
‎I'm worried about Yeo-ri.

343
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:16,296
‎Her grandmother is old and frail.

344
00:29:16,379 --> 00:29:18,173
‎I'm not sure she can handle the stress.

345
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:21,259
‎Have you paid Yeo-ri a visit?

346
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:23,094
‎No.

347
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,387
‎I couldn't bring myself to.

348
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:28,099
‎I understand.

349
00:29:28,683 --> 00:29:31,311
‎Going through something like this
‎is never easy.

350
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:34,230
‎Oh, excuse me.

351
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:38,485
‎Hello, Madam Pang.

352
00:29:39,903 --> 00:29:40,737
‎Pardon?

353
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:44,908
‎Is that so?

354
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:48,369
‎Yes.

355
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:51,456
‎You didn't pack things in order,
‎and now I have to reorganize them all.

356
00:29:51,539 --> 00:29:53,416
‎Then just organize it again.

357
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:54,918
‎You're talking back at me now?

358
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,378
‎That can go in here.

359
00:30:04,260 --> 00:30:05,970
‎You told me to go like it was no big deal.

360
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:10,809
‎Let's have a team dinner tonight.

361
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:12,352
‎I'll treat you to Korean beef. How's that?

362
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:15,396
‎Yes, Korean beef!
‎Investigator Ko, he'll buy us beef.

363
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:17,482
‎We can eat beef. Home-grown beef.

364
00:30:19,108 --> 00:30:20,443
‎What's up with you?

365
00:30:20,527 --> 00:30:22,403
‎It's not like he'll be gone forever.

366
00:30:22,487 --> 00:30:24,072
‎He'll be back soon.

367
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:26,074
‎We'll pretend
‎he's just on a long business trip.

368
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:28,451
‎Keep crying,
‎and we'll get pork rind instead.

369
00:30:29,035 --> 00:30:30,662
‎We're going to
‎the pork rind place tonight.

370
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:32,497
‎Fine. Korean beef it is.

371
00:30:32,580 --> 00:30:33,998
‎He said he wants Korean beef.

372
00:30:34,082 --> 00:30:35,750
‎-Let's go. Get up.
‎-Let's go.

373
00:30:35,834 --> 00:30:38,878
‎-I'm hungry.
‎-Let's go get some beef.

374
00:30:46,261 --> 00:30:47,679
‎What do you have to say
‎about the accident?

375
00:30:47,762 --> 00:30:50,348
‎I've yet to place a bigger bet.

376
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:53,017
‎I'll call you if that doesn't work out.

377
00:30:56,396 --> 00:30:57,647
‎Park Seung-jae…

378
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:59,399
‎I traced Park Seung-jae's movements,

379
00:30:59,482 --> 00:31:01,609
‎and he'd gone to his childhood home.

380
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:13,121
‎That's not cooked yet.
‎Eat this piece instead.

381
00:31:17,876 --> 00:31:19,502
‎You eat well for a guy
‎who was crying earlier.

382
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:21,713
‎I mean, it's beef. It's delicious.

383
00:31:21,796 --> 00:31:22,630
‎It is, right?

384
00:31:24,507 --> 00:31:25,967
‎So don't cry anymore, Investigator Ko.

385
00:31:26,050 --> 00:31:27,427
‎Here, cheers.

386
00:31:27,510 --> 00:31:29,137
‎No more tears, okay?

387
00:31:29,220 --> 00:31:30,513
‎-Cheers.
‎-Cheers.

388
00:31:35,685 --> 00:31:36,936
‎-Oh, right. Mr. Ma.
‎-Yeah?

389
00:31:37,020 --> 00:31:39,480
‎Ms. Cheon's much better now, right?

390
00:31:39,564 --> 00:31:40,440
‎Of course.

391
00:31:42,275 --> 00:31:43,735
‎I miss her all of a sudden.

392
00:31:44,485 --> 00:31:45,612
‎Why don't you call her?

393
00:31:45,695 --> 00:31:47,071
‎-Should I?
‎-Yes.

394
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:50,491
‎I've always wanted to call a girlfriend
‎during a work gathering.

395
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:53,995
‎Here.

396
00:31:56,039 --> 00:31:57,123
‎Hi, Gang-uk.

397
00:31:57,206 --> 00:31:58,374
‎Are you resting well, Yeo-ri?

398
00:31:59,000 --> 00:32:01,878
‎Yes, of course.
‎I'm getting plenty of rest.

399
00:32:02,378 --> 00:32:04,213
‎You can't overexert yourself, okay?

400
00:32:07,842 --> 00:32:09,761
‎-I just heard something.
‎-What?

401
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:11,054
‎-Oh…
‎-Are you outside?

402
00:32:11,137 --> 00:32:12,388
‎No, I'm…

403
00:32:13,014 --> 00:32:14,515
‎I came out for a walk.

404
00:32:14,599 --> 00:32:17,644
‎It was probably a car passing by
‎from over the fence.

405
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:21,064
‎But there aren't many cars
‎that drive by your house.

406
00:32:21,147 --> 00:32:24,484
‎Yes, but one just
‎happened to drive by just now.

407
00:32:25,068 --> 00:32:26,569
‎Accident-prone area ahead…

408
00:32:26,653 --> 00:32:27,946
‎I hear a GPS too.

409
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,447
‎No, you didn't.

410
00:32:29,530 --> 00:32:30,740
‎That was my TV.

411
00:32:30,823 --> 00:32:32,450
‎You just said you were out on a walk.

412
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:36,287
‎Yes, but I just got back inside.

413
00:32:36,371 --> 00:32:38,539
‎I'd forgotten to turn off the TV.

414
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:41,876
‎Yeo-ri, you can't risk any aftereffects.

415
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,003
‎So you shouldn't overdo it, okay?

416
00:32:44,087 --> 00:32:45,296
‎-What's wrong with him?
‎-He's so dramatic.

417
00:32:45,380 --> 00:32:47,507
‎I'll feed your fish for you too.

418
00:32:48,091 --> 00:32:48,925
‎Okay.

419
00:32:49,676 --> 00:32:50,760
‎You be careful too.

420
00:32:50,843 --> 00:32:51,803
‎Okay.

421
00:32:58,101 --> 00:32:59,644
‎She worries about me a lot.

422
00:32:59,727 --> 00:33:01,813
‎-Yeah, it seems like it.
‎-It sure does.

423
00:33:01,896 --> 00:33:02,939
‎Goodness.

424
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:04,524
‎Let's drink.

425
00:33:11,614 --> 00:33:12,782
‎-Pil-dong.
‎-Yeah?

426
00:33:12,865 --> 00:33:15,243
‎Call me as soon as
‎you get anything on Yeo-ri's case.

427
00:33:15,785 --> 00:33:18,496
‎I'd look into it myself
‎if I were in Seoul.

428
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:22,041
‎I know. I get the feeling
‎that the case is going nowhere.

429
00:33:22,625 --> 00:33:25,378
‎I asked around, but there were no updates.

430
00:33:26,004 --> 00:33:28,131
‎The public sentiment
‎has been pretty strange

431
00:33:28,798 --> 00:33:30,508
‎after Park Seung-jae died.

432
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:34,429
‎People are saying good riddance,
‎that he deserved to die.

433
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:42,645
‎Here's an idea.

434
00:33:42,729 --> 00:33:44,897
‎Let's make this
‎our last drink of the night

435
00:33:44,981 --> 00:33:46,649
‎-and call it a night.
‎-Okay.

436
00:33:46,733 --> 00:33:50,445
‎The two lovebirds are worried sick
‎about each other,

437
00:33:50,528 --> 00:33:52,488
‎-so we should cooperate.
‎-All right.

438
00:33:52,572 --> 00:33:53,448
‎There.

439
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:56,451
‎Besides, you have to start work
‎down south starting on Monday.

440
00:33:57,577 --> 00:33:59,162
‎-Cheers.
‎-We'll call it a night.

441
00:34:01,956 --> 00:34:04,208
‎You're staying with me for round two.

442
00:34:04,292 --> 00:34:05,209
‎Don't be ridiculous.

443
00:34:05,918 --> 00:34:07,879
‎I really need to get home early tonight.

444
00:34:09,756 --> 00:34:11,257
‎Okay, fine. No more tears.

445
00:34:18,181 --> 00:34:20,933
‎I have a feeling there's something here.

446
00:34:48,252 --> 00:34:49,754
‎Seung-jae's camcorder?

447
00:34:49,837 --> 00:34:51,089
‎LIST OF BELONGINGS

448
00:34:51,172 --> 00:34:54,008
‎ELECTRONICS, CAMCORDER, IN GOOD CONDITION

449
00:34:57,678 --> 00:34:59,138
‎It's missing the memory card.

450
00:35:45,476 --> 00:35:46,310
‎Who's there?

451
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:49,897
‎Gang-uk?

452
00:35:49,981 --> 00:35:51,399
‎Why are you here, Yeo-ri?

453
00:35:51,983 --> 00:35:53,276
‎What about you?

454
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:08,624
‎Sir, we've completed the preparations
‎for the memorial ceremony.

455
00:36:13,671 --> 00:36:16,841
‎Once I take over, I'll overhaul
‎the Office of Strategy and Planning first.

456
00:36:16,924 --> 00:36:18,885
‎I'll have you transferred there,

457
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:20,761
‎and you can serve as my control tower.

458
00:36:22,638 --> 00:36:23,681
‎Yes, sir.

459
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:26,350
‎Thank you for all your hard work.

460
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:27,602
‎Thank you, sir.

461
00:36:40,489 --> 00:36:43,242
‎-Thank you for coming.
‎-Of course I had to come.

462
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:46,245
‎You must be busy,
‎yet you've come two years in a row.

463
00:36:46,829 --> 00:36:48,664
‎-Ji-hwan would be so happy.
‎-Min-hwan.

464
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:51,250
‎-Excuse me.
‎-Sure.

465
00:36:51,834 --> 00:36:52,919
‎Thanks for coming.

466
00:36:53,002 --> 00:36:54,503
‎-Thank you for coming.
‎-Of course.

467
00:36:55,546 --> 00:36:56,380
‎So…

468
00:36:57,673 --> 00:37:00,801
‎I heard there will be
‎a very important announcement today.

469
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:02,261
‎Congratulations in advance.

470
00:37:04,972 --> 00:37:05,932
‎I'll see you after the memorial.

471
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:08,643
‎-I'll see you later.
‎-All right.

472
00:37:11,562 --> 00:37:12,855
‎It's true when they say

473
00:37:12,939 --> 00:37:14,690
‎the title makes the man.

474
00:37:14,774 --> 00:37:18,069
‎Don't you think he has
‎the air of a chairman today?

475
00:37:18,152 --> 00:37:19,028
‎Right?

476
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:25,826
‎Hello.

477
00:37:27,536 --> 00:37:29,455
‎It's been a while, Vice President Song.

478
00:37:30,998 --> 00:37:35,461
‎I hear a lot about you through your son,
‎CEO Kang Min-hwan.

479
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:37,922
‎Thank you for attending.

480
00:37:38,005 --> 00:37:38,839
‎Of course.

481
00:37:40,007 --> 00:37:42,468
‎Oh, you know my daughter Ha-ri.

482
00:37:42,969 --> 00:37:44,178
‎Hello, ma'am.

483
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,471
‎Welcome.

484
00:37:48,432 --> 00:37:50,393
‎We will now begin

485
00:37:50,476 --> 00:37:53,104
‎the twelfth memorial ceremony
‎for the late Kang Ji-hwan.

486
00:38:03,572 --> 00:38:04,573
‎We're gathered here today

487
00:38:05,324 --> 00:38:07,827
‎to remember my dear brother Ji-hwan,

488
00:38:07,910 --> 00:38:11,914
‎who left us too soon and unexpectedly.

489
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:16,460
‎Even though it's been a while
‎since he left us,

490
00:38:16,544 --> 00:38:18,754
‎I still can't believe he's gone.

491
00:38:19,422 --> 00:38:21,632
‎Although he was my younger brother,

492
00:38:21,716 --> 00:38:25,678
‎he was sometimes like an older brother,
‎and at other times, like a friend.

493
00:38:25,761 --> 00:38:28,097
‎He was always there
‎as a reliable companion.

494
00:38:28,639 --> 00:38:31,183
‎His presence alone was a great comfort.

495
00:38:32,059 --> 00:38:35,688
‎Ji-hwan left us all
‎with love and memories.

496
00:38:36,188 --> 00:38:37,982
‎That will remain with us in our lives

497
00:38:39,525 --> 00:38:41,068
‎and live on among us.

498
00:38:42,236 --> 00:38:43,237
‎Ji-hwan, my dear brother.

499
00:38:45,448 --> 00:38:46,490
‎I love you.

500
00:38:47,533 --> 00:38:48,534
‎And Mother,

501
00:38:49,785 --> 00:38:50,786
‎I love you.

502
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:57,501
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN'S
‎12TH MEMORIAL CEREMONY

503
00:39:03,507 --> 00:39:04,383
‎Let's speed up a little.

504
00:39:04,467 --> 00:39:05,384
‎Okay.

505
00:39:15,102 --> 00:39:16,103
‎Yes, I understand.

506
00:39:17,396 --> 00:39:18,272
‎I'm heading inside now.

507
00:39:22,693 --> 00:39:23,527
‎Who's there?

508
00:39:26,447 --> 00:39:27,823
‎Gang-uk?

509
00:39:27,907 --> 00:39:29,116
‎Why are you here, Yeo-ri?

510
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:30,993
‎What about you?

511
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:51,263
‎Just a moment.

512
00:39:52,932 --> 00:39:53,974
‎What brings you here?

513
00:39:56,018 --> 00:39:59,772
‎This is a search and seizure warrant
‎for Kang Ji-hwan's death 12 years ago.

514
00:40:13,994 --> 00:40:14,829
‎Today,

515
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,581
‎many of you graced this hall
‎with your presence.

516
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:25,214
‎I apologize for not being able to
‎thank each of you sincerely in person.

517
00:40:25,965 --> 00:40:26,757
‎Also,

518
00:40:27,883 --> 00:40:30,344
‎I will take to heart
‎the heartfelt condolences

519
00:40:31,178 --> 00:40:32,430
‎you have offered.

520
00:40:35,975 --> 00:40:39,770
‎All of you present are like family to us,

521
00:40:40,354 --> 00:40:43,774
‎so on behalf of CL's chairman
‎who is convalescing in the US,

522
00:40:44,525 --> 00:40:47,319
‎I would like to make
‎an important announcement

523
00:40:47,862 --> 00:40:50,948
‎concerning the future of CL Group.

524
00:40:52,199 --> 00:40:54,118
‎For the long-term future of our group,

525
00:40:54,201 --> 00:40:56,370
‎it is now time for young leadership

526
00:40:56,912 --> 00:40:59,373
‎as well as a new and different vision.

527
00:41:00,374 --> 00:41:03,627
‎So after a thorough discussion
‎with my family

528
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:05,754
‎and the board of directors--

529
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:06,839
‎Just a moment, please.

530
00:41:11,385 --> 00:41:12,219
‎Before that,

531
00:41:12,803 --> 00:41:14,597
‎there's something you should see.

532
00:41:15,598 --> 00:41:17,641
‎Yeo-ri. Are you all right?

533
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:21,937
‎My gosh, I thought she was in a coma.
‎What's she doing here?

534
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:24,315
‎I found a video

535
00:41:25,441 --> 00:41:28,152
‎that Ji-hwan left before he passed away.

536
00:41:29,195 --> 00:41:30,029
‎Will you see it?

537
00:41:31,322 --> 00:41:32,323
‎Is that true?

538
00:41:32,823 --> 00:41:33,949
‎Ji-hwan did?

539
00:41:35,284 --> 00:41:37,661
‎Ms. Cheon. What do you think you're doing?

540
00:41:37,745 --> 00:41:38,787
‎Min-hwan.

541
00:41:38,871 --> 00:41:39,705
‎Play it.

542
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:49,256
‎-Ji-hwan.
‎-Min-hwan!

543
00:41:50,925 --> 00:41:51,759
‎Min-hwan.

544
00:41:52,510 --> 00:41:54,345
‎Min-hwan, save me.

545
00:41:55,554 --> 00:41:57,890
‎Min-hwan, what's gotten into you?

546
00:41:57,973 --> 00:42:00,100
‎Min-hwan. No, don't let go.

547
00:42:00,893 --> 00:42:02,520
‎Min-hwan! Don't let go of my hand, okay?

548
00:42:02,603 --> 00:42:04,688
‎Min-hwan, no! No…

549
00:42:16,242 --> 00:42:17,201
‎Secretary Oh.

550
00:42:19,119 --> 00:42:20,037
‎Yes, ma'am.

551
00:42:20,663 --> 00:42:22,581
‎Escort the guests out of the hall

552
00:42:22,665 --> 00:42:25,584
‎and see that they have
‎no difficulty getting home.

553
00:42:26,210 --> 00:42:27,169
‎Yes, ma'am.

554
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:30,256
‎Today's memorial service has ended.

555
00:42:30,339 --> 00:42:31,382
‎-What?
‎-It's over?

556
00:42:31,465 --> 00:42:33,467
‎Allow us to escort you out of the hall.

557
00:42:34,051 --> 00:42:35,511
‎Please exit through the back door.

558
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:37,846
‎-What?
‎-Help me escort them outside.

559
00:42:38,389 --> 00:42:39,640
‎Goodbye then.

560
00:42:50,067 --> 00:42:51,068
‎Min-hwan!

561
00:42:53,320 --> 00:42:54,905
‎What did I just see?

562
00:42:55,489 --> 00:42:57,491
‎No… It's not what you think.

563
00:42:58,325 --> 00:42:59,451
‎Ms. Cheon.

564
00:43:00,035 --> 00:43:02,580
‎Where did you find that video?

565
00:43:03,247 --> 00:43:06,333
‎Park Seung-jae had filmed it
‎with his camcorder.

566
00:43:07,751 --> 00:43:10,421
‎I'm so sorry for causing you more pain.

567
00:43:12,756 --> 00:43:14,425
‎You don't believe what you saw, do you?

568
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:17,595
‎Until that video is authenticated,

569
00:43:18,512 --> 00:43:20,514
‎-lie low, Min-hwan.
‎-Mother.

570
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:24,101
‎Do you believe Cheon Yeo-ri

571
00:43:24,184 --> 00:43:26,145
‎and a video
‎that could be faked over me?

572
00:43:26,228 --> 00:43:27,980
‎It's not that I believe it.

573
00:43:28,606 --> 00:43:29,982
‎I'm saying we need confirmation.

574
00:43:32,651 --> 00:43:33,569
‎No.

575
00:43:36,196 --> 00:43:37,531
‎You don't believe me.

576
00:43:39,033 --> 00:43:40,242
‎Ever since I was young,

577
00:43:40,868 --> 00:43:42,828
‎you always believed
‎everything Ji-hwan said.

578
00:43:43,329 --> 00:43:44,413
‎So why don't you…

579
00:43:47,541 --> 00:43:49,418
‎ever believe what I say?

580
00:43:49,501 --> 00:43:50,544
‎Min-hwan.

581
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:54,381
‎I'll prove the truth to you.

582
00:43:59,386 --> 00:44:00,763
‎It's me.

583
00:44:00,846 --> 00:44:04,350
‎Call Attorney Park and have him
‎put together a team of his smartest.

584
00:44:04,433 --> 00:44:07,436
‎Defamation, spreading false information,
‎I'll sue for everything I can.

585
00:44:10,522 --> 00:44:11,607
‎Kang Min-hwan.

586
00:44:14,943 --> 00:44:16,403
‎You still have more?

587
00:44:17,196 --> 00:44:18,614
‎Why did you do it?

588
00:44:19,615 --> 00:44:20,824
‎Just why?

589
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:22,493
‎How could you…

590
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:25,704
‎do that to Ji-hwan?

591
00:44:29,416 --> 00:44:31,502
‎I'm sick of hearing his name.

592
00:44:32,711 --> 00:44:34,505
‎Do you even know what my life was like?

593
00:44:35,381 --> 00:44:38,300
‎People like you, born with everything,
‎could never understand

594
00:44:38,926 --> 00:44:41,095
‎what it's like
‎to forever be in someone's shadow.

595
00:44:42,680 --> 00:44:44,723
‎That's how I've lived my whole life.

596
00:44:44,807 --> 00:44:47,142
‎Falling behind,
‎having everything taken away, yearning!

597
00:44:50,062 --> 00:44:52,064
‎So I didn't want anything
‎taken away from me anymore.

598
00:44:53,857 --> 00:44:55,317
‎The company, my mother,

599
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:58,445
‎and you.

600
00:45:01,490 --> 00:45:02,699
‎But now, even you

601
00:45:03,450 --> 00:45:05,327
‎are coming after all I have?

602
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:06,328
‎No.

603
00:45:07,621 --> 00:45:09,081
‎I won't give up that easily.

604
00:45:15,629 --> 00:45:16,505
‎That was it?

605
00:45:18,215 --> 00:45:20,134
‎That's why you let Ji-hwan die,

606
00:45:21,718 --> 00:45:23,095
‎killed Park Seung-jae,

607
00:45:24,096 --> 00:45:25,389
‎and caused that truck accident?

608
00:45:26,265 --> 00:45:27,891
‎Do you think that justifies

609
00:45:28,892 --> 00:45:30,602
‎all the things you did?

610
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,229
‎How could you?

611
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:35,774
‎You only care about yourself.

612
00:45:37,025 --> 00:45:38,068
‎What about Ji-hwan?

613
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:42,489
‎What about all the years
‎he spent trusting you?

614
00:45:43,991 --> 00:45:46,994
‎Did that mean nothing to you?

615
00:45:48,495 --> 00:45:49,413
‎Did Ji-hwan say that?

616
00:45:51,498 --> 00:45:52,499
‎Is he here right now?

617
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,585
‎Kang Ji-hwan!

618
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:58,005
‎What did I do that was so wrong?

619
00:45:58,589 --> 00:46:00,632
‎Do you know
‎what I went through because of you

620
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:03,302
‎and how much I was looked down on?

621
00:46:04,261 --> 00:46:05,304
‎Do you?

622
00:46:05,387 --> 00:46:08,098
‎THE LATE KANG JI-HWAN

623
00:46:21,278 --> 00:46:22,321
‎Kang Min-hwan,

624
00:46:22,404 --> 00:46:24,490
‎you're under arrest
‎for the murder of Park Seung-jae.

625
00:46:24,573 --> 00:46:25,741
‎Listen.

626
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:27,868
‎What do you think you're doing?

627
00:46:27,951 --> 00:46:30,454
‎What does it look like?
‎We're carrying out official business.

628
00:46:30,954 --> 00:46:33,123
‎While you put on a show
‎planning the memorial,

629
00:46:33,207 --> 00:46:34,791
‎the police found
‎all the relevant evidence.

630
00:46:37,586 --> 00:46:38,587
‎Mr. Ma.

631
00:46:55,562 --> 00:46:56,480
‎Take him in.

632
00:46:58,190 --> 00:47:01,109
‎You have the right to an attorney,
‎the right to defend yourself,

633
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:03,820
‎-You can't do this. Let me go!
‎-and challenge your arrest.

634
00:47:03,904 --> 00:47:05,239
‎-Hold still.
‎-Let go!

635
00:47:07,407 --> 00:47:10,244
‎Ma Gang-uk, I'll make you pay for this.

636
00:47:10,327 --> 00:47:11,453
‎Got it?

637
00:47:12,079 --> 00:47:13,163
‎Let go of me!

638
00:47:14,039 --> 00:47:15,040
‎Damn it!

639
00:47:15,958 --> 00:47:16,875
‎Ma Gang-uk!

640
00:47:17,543 --> 00:47:18,794
‎It's not over yet!

641
00:47:19,545 --> 00:47:20,837
‎-Let me go!
‎-Are you okay?

642
00:47:20,921 --> 00:47:21,755
‎Hey!

643
00:47:22,256 --> 00:47:23,507
‎Let me go right now!

644
00:47:27,928 --> 00:47:29,263
‎We have a news flash.

645
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:30,597
‎Kang Min-hwan, CEO of CL Group,

646
00:47:30,681 --> 00:47:34,142
‎was just arrested
‎for the murder of Park Seung-jae,

647
00:47:34,226 --> 00:47:37,646
‎a former pro golfer
‎and son of late Assemblyman Park Jin-dong.

648
00:47:37,729 --> 00:47:39,022
‎The news shocked the public.

649
00:47:39,606 --> 00:47:43,318
‎Despite speculation on the motive
‎and circumstances of Park's death,

650
00:47:43,402 --> 00:47:46,697
‎CL Group has yet to release
‎an official statement,

651
00:47:46,780 --> 00:47:48,407
‎raising further questions.

652
00:47:51,994 --> 00:47:53,412
‎What do you think you're doing?

653
00:47:53,495 --> 00:47:55,706
‎-Director Ok Gye-hui?
‎-Yes, that's me.

654
00:47:55,789 --> 00:47:57,332
‎I'm Prosecutor Im Seo-hyeon
‎from the District Prosecutors' Office,

655
00:47:58,417 --> 00:48:00,168
‎and this is a search and seizure warrant.

656
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:03,547
‎It took us a while to get past
‎Chief Prosecutor Ok Gye-dong.

657
00:48:03,630 --> 00:48:06,258
‎Director Cheon Dong-jun's office
‎is being searched as we speak.

658
00:48:06,842 --> 00:48:08,927
‎Even Dong-jun? What now, Mom?

659
00:48:09,428 --> 00:48:12,389
‎Excuse me, everyone. Gentlemen?

660
00:48:12,472 --> 00:48:16,018
‎Is the district chief prosecutor
‎aware of this happening?

661
00:48:16,101 --> 00:48:17,644
‎Can you handle the aftermath?

662
00:48:18,228 --> 00:48:19,479
‎We're here because we can.

663
00:48:19,563 --> 00:48:20,647
‎Ms. Im.

664
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:21,982
‎No, not that!

665
00:48:22,065 --> 00:48:23,817
‎Don't touch that! Leave it alone!

666
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:25,694
‎You can't touch my safe!

667
00:48:25,777 --> 00:48:28,196
‎You must have something valuable inside.
‎Let's start with this.

668
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:32,326
‎You'd better hope my safe
‎is on the list of items to be seized.

669
00:48:32,409 --> 00:48:33,869
‎If it's not, you're all done for.

670
00:48:34,828 --> 00:48:35,912
‎Why can't I see the letters?

671
00:48:35,996 --> 00:48:39,291
‎Ha-ri, get my reading glasses.

672
00:48:39,374 --> 00:48:40,208
‎Mom.

673
00:48:40,292 --> 00:48:41,418
‎I can't read a thing.

674
00:48:42,711 --> 00:48:44,087
‎You'd better hope it's on this list.

675
00:48:45,422 --> 00:48:47,758
‎Gosh, why are the letters so blurry?
‎I can't see a thing.

676
00:48:47,841 --> 00:48:49,760
‎Why can't I read a word on this?

677
00:48:50,302 --> 00:48:51,219
‎Why can't I see anything?

678
00:48:51,845 --> 00:48:52,804
‎I still can't see…

679
00:48:53,847 --> 00:48:54,973
‎Mom!

680
00:48:55,057 --> 00:48:56,516
‎No! Mom!

681
00:48:57,392 --> 00:48:58,352
‎Mom!

682
00:48:58,935 --> 00:49:00,354
‎Mom, what's wrong?

683
00:49:00,437 --> 00:49:02,105
‎Stay with me, Mom. Mom!

684
00:49:02,189 --> 00:49:03,315
‎Ha-ri. Mom!

685
00:49:03,398 --> 00:49:05,609
‎Call an ambulance! Mom!

686
00:49:06,652 --> 00:49:13,659
‎1 YEAR LATER

687
00:49:21,291 --> 00:49:23,377
‎Hello, ma'am. How can I help you?

688
00:49:23,460 --> 00:49:24,711
‎I have a reservation.

689
00:49:24,795 --> 00:49:25,962
‎Can I have the name, please?

690
00:49:26,046 --> 00:49:27,255
‎It's Choi Seo-rin.

691
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:29,383
‎Choi Seo-rin…

692
00:49:29,466 --> 00:49:31,510
‎I need a coffee too.

693
00:49:34,137 --> 00:49:36,598
‎By the way, did you hear the rumor?

694
00:49:37,182 --> 00:49:38,141
‎What rumor?

695
00:49:38,850 --> 00:49:41,853
‎Oh, the rumor
‎that you're being promoted to director?

696
00:49:44,064 --> 00:49:45,440
‎-You heard?
‎-Of course.

697
00:49:45,524 --> 00:49:47,234
‎Weren't you the one who spread it?

698
00:49:47,317 --> 00:49:50,153
‎-It was all over the group chat.
‎-It's already spread that far?

699
00:49:51,488 --> 00:49:52,531
‎That's insane.

700
00:49:52,614 --> 00:49:54,449
‎Why? Isn't that a good thing?

701
00:49:54,533 --> 00:49:57,119
‎Yes, of course it's a good thing.
‎But you know what they say.

702
00:49:57,202 --> 00:49:59,287
‎"He who wants the crown

703
00:49:59,371 --> 00:50:01,164
‎must bear its weight."

704
00:50:02,582 --> 00:50:05,043
‎It's Reina Hotel's director
‎we're talking about.

705
00:50:05,127 --> 00:50:07,629
‎That comes with a huge sense
‎of responsibility and duty.

706
00:50:07,713 --> 00:50:09,548
‎Think of how heavy the weight will be.

707
00:50:09,631 --> 00:50:11,758
‎My shoulders are tensing up already.

708
00:50:12,718 --> 00:50:14,469
‎Just put on some pain relief patches then.

709
00:50:16,513 --> 00:50:18,849
‎Nothing could be heavier
‎than the weight I'm burdened with.

710
00:50:21,518 --> 00:50:22,394
‎Look at me.

711
00:50:23,186 --> 00:50:25,981
‎This is what happens when you lose
‎a power struggle in the royal family.

712
00:50:26,064 --> 00:50:27,649
‎Can you make me a coffee too?

713
00:50:34,406 --> 00:50:36,783
‎Excusez-moi,‎ Ms. Royal Family?

714
00:50:37,659 --> 00:50:41,621
‎I noticed the trash can
‎under the concierge desk

715
00:50:41,705 --> 00:50:43,123
‎was full and overflowing.

716
00:50:43,206 --> 00:50:45,125
‎Would you mind emptying it out?

717
00:50:46,918 --> 00:50:47,753
‎Right now.

718
00:50:50,130 --> 00:50:51,131
‎Okay.

719
00:50:54,843 --> 00:50:56,636
‎-Mom.
‎-Mom.

720
00:50:56,720 --> 00:50:59,097
‎Oh, Ha-ri, Dong-jun.

721
00:51:03,852 --> 00:51:07,022
‎It's hard work
‎being a concierge, isn't it?

722
00:51:07,898 --> 00:51:10,400
‎I'm doing what I'm told
‎and starting from rock bottom,

723
00:51:11,860 --> 00:51:12,736
‎but it's so hard.

724
00:51:12,819 --> 00:51:15,238
‎Hey, Cheon Ha-ri. Look at Mom.

725
00:51:15,989 --> 00:51:17,824
‎You're saying you have it hard
‎when she's in prison?

726
00:51:17,908 --> 00:51:19,785
‎The negligence and embezzlement…

727
00:51:20,410 --> 00:51:22,287
‎You're in here because
‎you took the fall for everything.

728
00:51:22,370 --> 00:51:25,248
‎You got off on probation,
‎so you need to be extra careful.

729
00:51:25,332 --> 00:51:26,541
‎I am being careful.

730
00:51:27,626 --> 00:51:29,920
‎And you, Ha-ri. Remember what I told you?

731
00:51:30,003 --> 00:51:32,631
‎Now that things have come to this, lie low

732
00:51:32,714 --> 00:51:34,257
‎and learn the ropes properly.

733
00:51:34,883 --> 00:51:39,262
‎Make sure that Chairwoman Cheon knows
‎you're working hard and diligently.

734
00:51:40,096 --> 00:51:41,723
‎-"Chairwoman Cheon"?
‎-Yeah.

735
00:51:41,807 --> 00:51:43,183
‎You mean Yeo-ri?

736
00:51:43,266 --> 00:51:47,187
‎Is there anyone else with that surname
‎who happens to be a chairwoman

737
00:51:47,270 --> 00:51:49,523
‎other than Chairwoman Cheon Yeo-ri?

738
00:51:51,024 --> 00:51:52,108
‎Listen.

739
00:51:52,192 --> 00:51:54,152
‎How you speak is a habit.

740
00:51:54,236 --> 00:51:57,864
‎You must practice saying the right thing
‎even when no one is looking.

741
00:51:57,948 --> 00:52:00,242
‎That way, you never make mistakes.

742
00:52:00,325 --> 00:52:02,494
‎Mom, what are you saying?

743
00:52:02,577 --> 00:52:04,871
‎Don't you know whose fault it is
‎that our lives are like this?

744
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:06,581
‎How can you even call her "chairwoman"?

745
00:52:06,665 --> 00:52:10,544
‎That's in the past.
‎We need to look ahead, all right?

746
00:52:10,627 --> 00:52:13,505
‎Hey, don't you know
‎how many Reina subsidiaries there are?

747
00:52:13,588 --> 00:52:17,467
‎Imagine how busy the chairwoman must be,
‎overseeing the entire group.

748
00:52:17,551 --> 00:52:20,929
‎If you gain the skills
‎and knowledge needed,

749
00:52:21,012 --> 00:52:24,474
‎she might even put you
‎in charge of Reina Hotel.

750
00:52:24,558 --> 00:52:26,142
‎Do you really think so?

751
00:52:26,226 --> 00:52:27,727
‎It's hard to ignore a blood relative.

752
00:52:27,811 --> 00:52:31,481
‎Why do you think your grandma
‎chose Chairwoman Cheon over us?

753
00:52:31,565 --> 00:52:32,440
‎In the end,

754
00:52:32,524 --> 00:52:35,443
‎everyone gives in to blood, got it?

755
00:52:35,527 --> 00:52:36,820
‎You really think so?

756
00:52:36,903 --> 00:52:37,946
‎Of course.

757
00:52:38,029 --> 00:52:41,116
‎So you behave well, Dong-jun.

758
00:52:41,199 --> 00:52:43,827
‎Stay loyal to Chairwoman Cheon, okay?

759
00:52:44,411 --> 00:52:45,996
‎Okay. I'll stay loyal.

760
00:52:53,044 --> 00:52:54,045
‎Yeo-ri!

761
00:53:12,355 --> 00:53:13,773
‎You came here without a call?

762
00:53:13,857 --> 00:53:15,525
‎What are you doing here?

763
00:53:15,609 --> 00:53:18,278
‎-I missed you so much.
‎-So did I.

764
00:53:19,195 --> 00:53:20,614
‎I hope nothing's wrong.

765
00:53:20,697 --> 00:53:22,532
‎So this is what it feels like.

766
00:53:22,616 --> 00:53:23,742
‎What do you mean?

767
00:53:23,825 --> 00:53:26,411
‎You're always springing surprises on me,

768
00:53:26,494 --> 00:53:27,954
‎so I wanted to try it for a change.

769
00:53:29,039 --> 00:53:29,873
‎So how does it feel?

770
00:53:32,709 --> 00:53:34,544
‎It's just the same as any other day.

771
00:53:37,130 --> 00:53:40,675
‎I attended an event
‎at Reina Hotel in Gyeongju.

772
00:53:40,759 --> 00:53:43,553
‎I was supposed to
‎head back to Seoul right after,

773
00:53:43,637 --> 00:53:44,763
‎but I stopped by to see you.

774
00:53:45,972 --> 00:53:48,308
‎We must have some kind of connection.

775
00:53:48,391 --> 00:53:49,476
‎I had something to say.

776
00:53:49,559 --> 00:53:50,477
‎What is it?

777
00:53:50,560 --> 00:53:53,104
‎I'm returning to Seoul. I got promoted.

778
00:53:53,688 --> 00:53:55,649
‎Really? When do you come back?

779
00:53:55,732 --> 00:53:58,318
‎It was announced today,
‎so some time in the next ten days?

780
00:53:59,194 --> 00:54:00,028
‎Really?

781
00:54:02,280 --> 00:54:05,033
‎I'm more pleased
‎that you're happy about it

782
00:54:05,116 --> 00:54:06,618
‎than the fact that I got promoted.

783
00:54:06,701 --> 00:54:08,578
‎Let's go on dates every day
‎once I return to Seoul.

784
00:54:09,329 --> 00:54:10,872
‎-Then tomorrow…
‎-Yes?

785
00:54:11,414 --> 00:54:12,958
‎To celebrate your promotion,

786
00:54:13,959 --> 00:54:16,044
‎how about we go on a date here in Andong?

787
00:54:16,628 --> 00:54:17,879
‎Can we do that?

788
00:54:18,421 --> 00:54:20,715
‎I only got to see you briefly so far.

789
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:24,344
‎Then I'll take tomorrow off.

790
00:54:24,886 --> 00:54:28,181
‎I'd been meaning to
‎check out a few places here.

791
00:54:28,264 --> 00:54:30,558
‎I held off so I could go with you.

792
00:54:30,642 --> 00:54:32,894
‎-Where?
‎-To see some traditional houses,

793
00:54:33,395 --> 00:54:34,938
‎and maybe a masked dance?

794
00:54:35,522 --> 00:54:36,564
‎We can eat at nice restaurants

795
00:54:36,648 --> 00:54:38,233
‎and see the sunset together.

796
00:54:38,316 --> 00:54:41,236
‎Just thinking about
‎doing all that with you makes me happy.

797
00:54:42,654 --> 00:54:43,488
‎Right now?

798
00:54:43,571 --> 00:54:45,991
‎Right now? Okay. Let's go.

799
00:54:46,074 --> 00:54:47,575
‎-Let's go then.
‎-Okay.

800
00:54:48,660 --> 00:54:50,453
‎How about you get on the back of my bike?

801
00:54:55,208 --> 00:54:56,292
‎-This is fun.
‎-It's fun?

802
00:54:56,376 --> 00:54:57,377
‎Yes.

803
00:54:57,460 --> 00:54:59,129
‎Do I weigh that much though?

804
00:54:59,212 --> 00:55:00,505
‎Why are you going so slow?

805
00:55:00,588 --> 00:55:01,881
‎I'm not.

806
00:55:01,965 --> 00:55:03,591
‎This isn't an electric bike.

807
00:55:04,718 --> 00:55:06,845
‎Are you holding on tight, Yeo-ri?

808
00:55:08,471 --> 00:55:10,098
‎Oh, careful. Careful.

809
00:55:11,057 --> 00:55:14,185
‎CORRECTIONAL SERVICES
‎ADVANCING ORDER AND HUMAN RIGHTS

810
00:55:40,503 --> 00:55:41,504
‎Why did you

811
00:55:42,172 --> 00:55:44,674
‎refuse my visits all this time?

812
00:55:46,342 --> 00:55:47,969
‎Didn't you miss me?

813
00:55:52,974 --> 00:55:54,017
‎I was afraid.

814
00:55:57,187 --> 00:55:59,439
‎I feared the way you'd look at me…

815
00:56:02,525 --> 00:56:04,235
‎now that you know what I did to Ji-hwan.

816
00:56:06,654 --> 00:56:08,865
‎If you don't want to terminate
‎Min-hwan's adoption,

817
00:56:09,491 --> 00:56:11,326
‎send him abroad to study
‎as soon as possible.

818
00:56:12,243 --> 00:56:13,703
‎I've seen many people like him.

819
00:56:14,329 --> 00:56:17,540
‎They bite the hand that fed them
‎once they grow up.

820
00:56:18,249 --> 00:56:21,461
‎Ji-hwan loves his brother.

821
00:56:21,544 --> 00:56:24,714
‎And Min-hwan takes
‎good care of Ji-hwan too.

822
00:56:25,381 --> 00:56:27,717
‎Mother, don't forget that Min-hwan

823
00:56:28,551 --> 00:56:31,221
‎is also a member of this family.

824
00:56:33,264 --> 00:56:34,307
‎I'm sorry.

825
00:56:38,812 --> 00:56:39,646
‎Min-hwan.

826
00:56:42,524 --> 00:56:45,401
‎This is what I think.

827
00:56:47,320 --> 00:56:48,321
‎One day,

828
00:56:49,572 --> 00:56:52,492
‎after you've paid the price
‎for your wrongdoings

829
00:56:53,409 --> 00:56:55,453
‎and are ready to rejoin society,

830
00:56:56,663 --> 00:56:59,332
‎if you have nowhere else to turn to…

831
00:57:01,000 --> 00:57:02,043
‎I think

832
00:57:03,920 --> 00:57:06,339
‎I'd be able to welcome you back.

833
00:57:08,383 --> 00:57:09,717
‎Whenever that may be.

834
00:57:42,792 --> 00:57:43,918
‎Come give me a hug,

835
00:57:44,002 --> 00:57:47,255
‎our new deputy chief prosecutor.

836
00:57:52,302 --> 00:57:53,261
‎You've heard, right?

837
00:57:54,179 --> 00:57:56,598
‎The entire leadership here
‎has been replaced.

838
00:57:56,681 --> 00:57:58,224
‎-So I heard.
‎-Did you also hear

839
00:57:58,308 --> 00:58:01,186
‎that the new prosecutor general
‎picked you out himself

840
00:58:01,269 --> 00:58:02,562
‎to have you work directly for him?

841
00:58:03,688 --> 00:58:05,148
‎He's a great judge of character.

842
00:58:06,483 --> 00:58:07,525
‎I'm so envious.

843
00:58:08,151 --> 00:58:11,488
‎Anyone I side with gets fired,
‎demoted, or whatever.

844
00:58:11,571 --> 00:58:14,240
‎Every connection I make
‎is the worst connection ever.

845
00:58:14,741 --> 00:58:17,911
‎How do you gain powerful connections
‎when you don't do anything?

846
00:58:17,994 --> 00:58:21,206
‎Who said I don't do anything?
‎I work hard, okay?

847
00:58:21,873 --> 00:58:22,790
‎By the book.

848
00:58:23,791 --> 00:58:24,709
‎"By the book."

849
00:58:27,295 --> 00:58:29,881
‎-I'm back!
‎-Long time no see.

850
00:58:29,964 --> 00:58:30,840
‎I said I'm back.

851
00:58:30,924 --> 00:58:33,718
‎-Where did it go?
‎-It must be here somewhere.

852
00:58:33,801 --> 00:58:35,220
‎Why are you ignoring me?

853
00:58:35,303 --> 00:58:36,304
‎This is something important.

854
00:58:36,387 --> 00:58:38,014
‎-Where is it?
‎-What's so important?

855
00:58:38,097 --> 00:58:39,849
‎Where did we put it? Is it behind this?

856
00:58:41,059 --> 00:58:43,603
‎CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR PROMOTION
‎DEPUTY CHIEF PROSECUTOR

857
00:58:43,686 --> 00:58:45,271
‎Mr. Ma!

858
00:58:48,525 --> 00:58:49,776
‎Careful, careful.

859
00:58:49,859 --> 00:58:52,028
‎-I like your new style.
‎-Deputy Chief Prosecutor!

860
00:58:52,111 --> 00:58:53,530
‎That hairstyle makes you look older.

861
00:58:53,613 --> 00:58:56,824
‎-This look is trending nowadays.
‎-Are you sure about that?

862
00:58:56,908 --> 00:59:00,245
‎It was too short a while
‎to call it a short while.

863
00:59:00,328 --> 00:59:01,246
‎I told you, didn't I?

864
00:59:01,329 --> 00:59:04,457
‎That he'd return with a promotion
‎before his two-year term was up.

865
00:59:04,541 --> 00:59:05,750
‎-That I did.
‎-Mr. Ma.

866
00:59:05,833 --> 00:59:08,002
‎I've lost weight because
‎we haven't had any team dinners.

867
00:59:08,586 --> 00:59:09,837
‎-You sure?
‎-You look the same.

868
00:59:09,921 --> 00:59:11,965
‎I look the same, but I've lost weight.

869
00:59:12,674 --> 00:59:16,177
‎Anyway, let's make up for all the dinners
‎with a party today. Deal?

870
00:59:16,261 --> 00:59:18,513
‎-Deal.
‎-Deal.

871
00:59:18,596 --> 00:59:19,889
‎But before that,

872
00:59:19,973 --> 00:59:21,307
‎we must work.

873
00:59:22,350 --> 00:59:23,476
‎-Okay.
‎-Okay.

874
00:59:23,560 --> 00:59:25,270
‎Now, let's get to it!

875
00:59:25,979 --> 00:59:27,397
‎This is yours.

876
00:59:28,898 --> 00:59:31,859
‎-I'll take… Okay.
‎-Bring those over here.

877
00:59:31,943 --> 00:59:33,570
‎I'll start with this much.

878
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:34,779
‎Okay.

879
00:59:35,530 --> 00:59:38,616
‎This stack should last us a few years.

880
00:59:38,700 --> 00:59:39,617
‎Don't you think so?

881
00:59:41,661 --> 00:59:42,704
‎What should we eat today?

882
00:59:44,539 --> 00:59:46,499
‎Where should we go for our first round?

883
00:59:46,583 --> 00:59:49,002
‎The Parents' Day Special
‎is being very well received.

884
00:59:49,085 --> 00:59:51,379
‎-Is everything going smoothly?
‎-Absolutely.

885
00:59:51,462 --> 00:59:52,922
‎Everything's going…

886
00:59:56,634 --> 00:59:57,844
‎Are you okay?

887
00:59:57,927 --> 00:59:59,679
‎Oh, dear. I'm sorry.

888
01:00:04,392 --> 01:00:07,103
‎Let's get you up. One, two. There you go.

889
01:00:08,313 --> 01:00:09,147
‎I'm sorry.

890
01:00:09,230 --> 01:00:10,940
‎-It's fine.
‎-Thank you.

891
01:00:11,524 --> 01:00:12,358
‎Take care.

892
01:00:12,942 --> 01:00:13,985
‎Bye.

893
01:00:22,035 --> 01:00:23,161
‎Oh, where was I?

894
01:00:23,244 --> 01:00:25,747
‎-The Parents' Day Special.
‎-Right, let's go.

895
01:00:26,331 --> 01:00:27,957
‎It's good to see you all.

896
01:00:28,041 --> 01:00:30,084
‎INAUGURATION OF REINA GROUP'S CHAIRWOMAN

897
01:00:30,168 --> 01:00:32,086
‎You would agree that Reina Group

898
01:00:32,170 --> 01:00:34,881
‎has been through a lot
‎in the past few years.

899
01:00:34,964 --> 01:00:36,174
‎We've had some tough times.

900
01:00:37,592 --> 01:00:39,719
‎Despite all that,

901
01:00:39,802 --> 01:00:42,889
‎our group has maintained
‎its position at the top.

902
01:00:42,972 --> 01:00:47,268
‎Now, as we are about to
‎take an evolutionary leap,

903
01:00:47,852 --> 01:00:49,771
‎we need a new leader.

904
01:00:50,813 --> 01:00:52,940
‎Someone with a delicate touch and insight

905
01:00:53,024 --> 01:00:56,944
‎who has also proven to be a strong leader
‎and can take action when necessary.

906
01:00:58,071 --> 01:00:59,614
‎I wish to appoint CEO Cheon Yeo-ri

907
01:00:59,697 --> 01:01:02,617
‎as the new chairwoman of Reina Group.

908
01:01:56,587 --> 01:01:58,089
‎-On the day we got engaged,
‎-Yes?

909
01:01:59,298 --> 01:02:02,009
‎do you remember asking me
‎what I wanted to do?

910
01:02:02,093 --> 01:02:03,177
‎Of course I remember.

911
01:02:04,178 --> 01:02:07,557
‎You said you wanted to walk hand-in-hand
‎with the person you liked.

912
01:02:09,308 --> 01:02:13,020
‎I wondered back then
‎whether that day would ever come.

913
01:02:13,730 --> 01:02:17,150
‎But now, the future I dreamed of
‎has become a reality.

914
01:02:17,775 --> 01:02:18,609
‎It has.

915
01:02:20,403 --> 01:02:21,946
‎Back then,

916
01:02:22,029 --> 01:02:24,115
‎something mundane for everyone else

917
01:02:24,866 --> 01:02:28,202
‎felt almost like a miracle to us.

918
01:02:30,913 --> 01:02:31,831
‎So miracles

919
01:02:33,207 --> 01:02:34,667
‎have become our everyday life.

920
01:02:37,795 --> 01:02:39,046
‎Then what should

921
01:02:39,630 --> 01:02:41,340
‎our next miracle be?

922
01:03:45,905 --> 01:03:48,282
‎SPOOKY IN LOVE

923
01:03:49,033 --> 01:03:50,785
‎-Is this the first scene?
‎-Yes.

924
01:03:50,868 --> 01:03:52,078
‎-The main… Okay.
‎-Yes.

925
01:03:52,912 --> 01:03:55,873
‎-I look forward to working with you all!
‎-Okay!

926
01:03:57,875 --> 01:03:58,709
‎Ma'am?

927
01:03:58,793 --> 01:03:59,836
‎Here's the drink…

928
01:04:00,628 --> 01:04:02,129
‎I mean, the information. Darn it.

929
01:04:03,464 --> 01:04:05,550
‎Life is very precious
‎if you think about it.

930
01:04:07,468 --> 01:04:08,928
‎-Darn it.
‎-Hey…

931
01:04:09,512 --> 01:04:10,721
‎Am I being too sensitive?

932
01:04:16,686 --> 01:04:18,020
‎Of course I'll be okay.

933
01:04:21,899 --> 01:04:23,317
‎If you get the case, you'd win…

934
01:04:24,819 --> 01:04:26,821
‎-I'm sorry, let me try that again.
‎-One more time.

935
01:04:26,904 --> 01:04:28,281
‎Act natural.

936
01:04:28,990 --> 01:04:32,451
‎I located the taxi
‎and emailed you the details…

937
01:04:32,535 --> 01:04:33,870
‎Darn it. I'm sorry.

938
01:04:33,953 --> 01:04:35,746
‎Your muscles are so tense.

939
01:04:37,540 --> 01:04:38,541
‎Cut!

940
01:04:44,255 --> 01:04:46,382
‎Don't forget that I have your back.

941
01:04:47,550 --> 01:04:48,885
‎Don't you ever…

942
01:04:49,510 --> 01:04:50,553
‎Got it?

943
01:04:53,055 --> 01:04:55,057
‎Yeo-ri…

944
01:04:57,602 --> 01:04:58,728
‎Let me try that again.

945
01:05:00,771 --> 01:05:01,981
‎But don't let it show.

946
01:05:03,649 --> 01:05:04,609
‎What was it?

947
01:05:05,943 --> 01:05:06,861
‎What is it?

948
01:05:07,695 --> 01:05:08,654
‎Wait, hold on.

949
01:05:08,738 --> 01:05:11,824
‎If you had a time machine,
‎where would you…

950
01:05:13,326 --> 01:05:14,243
‎This is driving me crazy.

951
01:05:21,459 --> 01:05:22,293
‎One more time.

952
01:05:23,878 --> 01:05:24,962
‎Chug it down.

953
01:05:25,046 --> 01:05:26,923
‎Oh gosh, don't spit it out…

954
01:05:30,509 --> 01:05:31,344
‎I need to tuck it all back.

955
01:05:32,011 --> 01:05:33,846
‎Strolling with the man…

956
01:05:37,808 --> 01:05:39,560
‎I love you, Team ‎Spooky in Love‎.

957
01:05:39,644 --> 01:05:40,728
‎I love you.

958
01:05:41,228 --> 01:05:43,272
‎Dear production staff,
‎thanks for all your hard work!

959
01:05:43,356 --> 01:05:44,649
‎-Thank you!
‎-Thank you!

960
01:05:47,610 --> 01:05:49,153
‎PARK EUN-BIN

961
01:05:49,236 --> 01:05:50,780
‎YANG SE-JONG

962
01:05:50,863 --> 01:05:52,406
‎ONG SEONG-WU

963
01:05:52,490 --> 01:05:54,033
‎JO HYE-JOO

964
01:05:54,116 --> 01:05:55,660
‎KIM DO-WAN

965
01:05:55,743 --> 01:05:57,286
‎YE SOO-JUNG

966
01:05:57,370 --> 01:05:58,913
‎CHA MI-KYEONG

967
01:05:58,996 --> 01:06:00,539
‎KIM SO-RA

968
01:06:00,623 --> 01:06:02,166
‎LEE JUN-HYEOK

969
01:06:02,249 --> 01:06:03,793
‎BAIK JI-WON

970
01:06:03,876 --> 01:06:05,419
‎LEE CHANG-HOON

